                <pb facs="0514" n="1474" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1474"/>

                <head>No. 999.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Magee to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 16, 1888</date>.
                        (Received February 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 110.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On last Friday, the 13th instant, the board
                    of trade for Sweden issued a decree forbidding the Importation of American pork
                    into this Kingdom, except that the same be well salted and cured.</p>
                <p>I have no information on the subject, but I presume that the board of trade for
                    Norway has or will issue a similar decree.</p>
                <p>The issuance of this decree is the result of information received at the foreign
                    department from the Swedish Norwegian minister at Washington that American pork
                    is infected with contagious disease.</p>
                <p>Such a disease, or a disease of an infectious character, has prevailed among
                    swine herds in the two kingdoms for some time and the board is taking very
                    active measures to stamp it out.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rufus Magee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
